  "description": "T1\tFalse Acacia x 1 (Robinia pseudoacacia) \rT2\tFalse Acacia x 1 (Robinia pseudoacacia) \rS2\tFalse Acacia x 1 (Robinia pseudoacacia) \rT3\tOlive x 1\t(Olea europaea)\t\r\rCouncil Note\r\rThe submission includes proposed works to trees in a conservation area and indicates that consent is also sought for a tree protected by a Tree Preservation Order. TPO 406 identifies a false acacia in the rear garden. The submitted plan and description do not clearly distinguish the protected tree from the other trees or adequately specify all proposed works. The Council has recorded this case as withdrawn in Uniform. No no-objection outcome has been issued. The applicant has been asked to submit a clearly identified TPO application and, where required, a separate section 211 notice.",
